cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this workflow, please cite it with these metadata. To cite the
  knowledge graph itself, cite its record on Zenodo, given in the README and on
  the website.
type: software
title: Workflow of the Climate Change Knowledge Graph
abstract: >-
  The workflow (Snakemake, jq, Apache Jena) that builds the Climate Change
  Knowledge Graph (CCKG) from its sources, with the mappings, the content
  curated by hand, the SHACL shapes, the queries checking the KG and the
  website documenting it. The CCKG describes the climate variables (CF
  standard names, MIP variables of the CMOR tables, climate indices), the
  climate models and the simulations of CMIP5 and CORDEX-CMIP5 with their
  datasets, the UKCP18 datasets, the emissions scenarios and global warming
  levels, and the controlled vocabularies of hazards, methods and operations
  of climate services, described with the HACID ontologies (top-level, data
  and CCSO). Every source is taken at a fixed version, so that each release
  of the KG can be rebuilt from the same inputs. It was first developed in
  the European project HACID (Hybrid Human Artificial Collective Intelligence
  in Open-Ended Decision Making, Horizon Europe grant 101070588).
